  "facts": [
    "The Mike O'Callaghan–Pat Tillman Memorial Bridge, opened in 2010, was the first concrete‑steel composite deck arch bridge in the United States, featuring the widest concrete arch in the Western Hemisphere.",
    "Standing 890 feet above the Colorado River, the bridge is the highest road bridge in the U.S. and the tallest on the Interstate Highway System, surpassing even the Royal Gorge Bridge for vehicular traffic.",
    "Constructed as part of the Hoover Dam Bypass, the bridge rerouted US 93 away from the dangerous, congested route over Hoover Dam, eliminating hairpin turns and blind curves that had plagued travelers since the 1930s."
